# AI guardrails

## The six permitted AI jobs
1. question_rationale — explain why a question matters
2. policy_simplifier — simplify a guidance concept
3. suggested_wording — draft empathetic resident-facing wording
4. wrap_up_summary — generate structured case note draft
5. coaching_feedback — generate after-call coaching
6. missed_support_opportunity — detect likely missed signposting

## Rules for every AI job
- Each job has its own prompt template file in src/ai/tasks/
- All outputs are schema-validated before use
- All outputs include a confidence field
- Source content is bounded to session_facts, workflow_trace, public_policy snippets, acme_operations snippets
- The model does not use background knowledge for policy or local rules
- Every AI output records prompt_version_id and model_name

## Forbidden AI behaviors
- claiming legal entitlement
- inventing council policy rules
- overriding escalation logic
- fabricating missing facts
- presenting guesses as confirmed policy

## Fallback requirement
Every AI job must have a deterministic fallback that activates when:
- the AI service is unavailable
- the output fails schema validation
- the output confidence is below the threshold
